    "title": "FIFA World Cup 2026 playoffs: Bolivia rallies to beat Suriname, Jamaica reaches final",
    "text": "Bolivia's Miguel Terceros celebrates after scoring his side’s second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 inter-confederation playoff match against Suriname. | Photo Credit: REUTERS Bolivia's Miguel Terceros celebrates after scoring his side’s second goal during the FIFA World Cup 2026 inter-confederation playoff match against Suriname. | Photo Credit: REUTERS Bolivia came from behind to beat Suriname 2-1 ​in their inter-confederation playoff semifinal in Monterrey ‌on Thursday, keeping alive its ​hopes of a first World ⁠Cup appearance since 1994.The South Americans will face Iraq in Tuesday’s playoff final for ‌a place at the tournament in Group I, while Suriname’s ‌bid to reach the finals for ‌the ⁠first time came to an ⁠end after surrendering its early second-half lead.Suriname struck three minutes after the restart when Liam ​van Gelderen reacted ‌quickest to a chaotic goalmouth scramble, pouncing on a loose ball after keeper Guillermo Viscarra failed to gather ‌or clear and tapping home from ​close range.ALSO READ | FIFA World Cup playoffs: Gyokeres hat-trick helps Sweden beat Ukraine; Turkey edges past RomaniaPowered by:Substitute Moises Paniagua drew Bolivia level in the 72nd ⁠minute, latching onto a loose ball after a series of deflections and steering ‌a toe-poked finish into the far corner.Bolivia was then awarded a penalty after a Myenty Abena foul on Juan Godoy, and Miguel Terceros stepped up to convert from the ‌spot in the 79th minute, completing the turnaround ​for ‘La Verde’.Played in front of a largely Bolivian crowd at ⁠Monterrey’s Estadio BBVA, the match was attended ⁠by FIFA president Gianni Infantino and offered a glimpse of a ‌venue set to host four games at the World Cup.Jamaica registers 1-0 win over New CaledoniaMeanwhile, Jamaica defeated New Caledonia 1-0 in Guadalajara to keep alive its ​hopes of a first ⁠World Cup appearance since 1998.Jamaica will face DR Congo on Tuesday for ‌a spot in Group K at the June ‌11 to July 19 ‌World ⁠Cup in North America ⁠alongside Colombia, Portugal, and Uzbekistan, while New Caledonia’s hunt for its first finals ​berth came ‌to an end. Jamaica's Bailey-Tye Cadamarteri celebrates scoring the side’s first goal with Richard King. | Photo Credit: REUTERS Jamaica's Bailey-Tye Cadamarteri celebrates scoring the side’s first goal with Richard King. | Photo Credit: REUTERS Jamaica’s Bailey Cadamarteri scored the only goal in the 18th minute, converting from ‌close range after New Caledonia ​keeper parried Ronaldo Webster’s free kick into his ⁠path.Georges Gope-Fenepej had a golden opportunity to equalise early in the ‌second half but could not connect with a cross in front of goal.New Caledonia keeper Rocky Nyikeine made a crucial intervention to halt ‌Webster’s dangerous run inside the box and ​prevent Jamaica from doubling its lead.The crowd got ⁠behind New Caledonia as it pushed ⁠for a late equaliser, but the side could not break ‌through, and Jamaica closed out the win.Published on Mar 27, 2026",
